[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/14918","id":5141713809,"node_id":"PR_kwDODKw3uc8AAAABMnhTkQ","html_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14918","diff_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14918.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14918.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/issues/14918","number":14918,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Clarify which hosts use GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN","user":{"login":"BagToad","id":47394200,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3Mzk0MjAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47394200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad","html_url":"https://github.com/BagToad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"<!--\nThank you for contributing to GitHub CLI!\n\nIf you are proposing a fix for a security issue, STOP and follow .github/SECURITY.md instead.\n\nKeep the entire pull request self-contained, reviewer-facing, and diegetic: describe the\nchange, rationale, and evidence within the context of the repository and pull request. Do not\nnarrate how the pull request was produced or refer to private conversations, prior agent work,\nor other behind-the-scenes context. Omit those details unless they materially affect review;\nif they do, state the relevant fact and its significance directly.\n-->\n\n<!-- List related issues here. Use `fixes` or `closes` keywords to associate an issue number. -->\n\n### Description\n\n<!--\nWhat's the problem? How are we addressing it?\n\nWrite for a reviewer who has not worked in this part of the codebase. Give them the\nbackground they need before the problem makes sense, and avoid jargon.\n-->\n\nOur help text doesn't say which hosts get `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`. go-gh's [`tokenForHost`](https://github.com/cli/go-gh/blob/v2.17.0/pkg/auth/auth.go#L63-L84) gives `GH_TOKEN` to `github.com`, subdomains of `ghe.com`, and `github.localhost`. Every other host [counts as GitHub Enterprise Server](https://github.com/cli/go-gh/blob/v2.17.0/pkg/auth/auth.go#L159-L166) and gets `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`. This PR clarifies this in [`gh help environment`](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/7e97c4c4f5124f5e74611c099a610989315f128b/pkg/cmd/root/help_topic.go#L45-L50) and [`gh api --help`](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/7e97c4c4f5124f5e74611c099a610989315f128b/pkg/cmd/api/api.go#L221-L225).\n\n### How did you test this change?\n\n<!--\nReport only actions you actually performed and results you actually observed, using factual\nfirst-person language (for example, \"I ran...\" and \"I saw...\"). Do not present planned,\nhypothetical, inferred, or merely expected scenarios as testing.\n\nAutomated test results do not belong here. Passing unit tests, `go test ./...` output, and\ncoverage numbers tell a reviewer nothing they cannot see from CI, so do not paste them.\n\nIf you did not exercise the changed behavior, write `Not tested` and explain why.\n\nUse one or more of these, whichever communicates best:\n\n1. Screenshots or GIFs of the real command running. Preferred whenever the change is visible\n   in terminal output. If output changed, show it before and after.\n2. Given/When/Then scenarios, but only when you actually executed the steps. For example:\n   Given I was in a repo with no open pull requests\n   When I ran `gh pr list`\n   Then I saw \"no open pull requests in cli/cli\"\n3. A natural language walkthrough of what you did by hand, the states you covered, and what\n   you saw, including error and edge cases.\n\nIf you leave this empty, your pull request will very likely be closed.\n-->\n\nI built `gh` from trunk and this branch. Here's the `gh help environment` enterprise entry before and after:\n\n```diff\n `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` (in order of precedence): an authentication\n-token that will be used when a command targets a GitHub Enterprise Server host.\n+token that will be used when a command targets a GitHub Enterprise Server host. `gh` treats any host other\n+than `github.com`, a subdomain of `ghe.com`, or `github.localhost` as a GitHub Enterprise Server host.\n```\n\n`gh api --help` changed to match. Then I set `GH_TOKEN` and `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` to different fake values. On both builds, `gh auth token --hostname` picked `GH_TOKEN` for `github.com`, `acme.ghe.com`, and `github.localhost`, and `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` for `github.example.com`.\n\n### Key points\n\n<!--\nTradeoffs you accepted, alternatives you rejected, and anything a reviewer would otherwise have to guess at.\n-->\n\n- I included `github.localhost` because go-gh gives it `GH_TOKEN` too.\n- I left out subdomains like `api.github.com`, which go-gh [maps to the parent host](https://github.com/cli/go-gh/blob/v2.17.0/pkg/auth/auth.go#L178-L185).\n\n### Notes for reviewers\n\n<!--\nWhere should review start, and what should be read next? Call out anything you are unsure about.\n\nLink related issues or prior discussion, with one sentence on why each matters.\n-->\n\n[#9809](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/9809) last reworked these entries.\n\n### Authorship and follow-up\n\n<!--\nREQUIRED - If you are an AI agent filling in this template, answer \"Who wrote this\" for yourself and answer honestly. For \"Who answers review comments,\" use only a choice the human has explicitly made in the conversation. If no choice has already been established, pause and ask the human to choose one of the three options before creating or updating the pull request. Do not infer the choice from repository ownership, authorship, assignees, prior interactions, or the current operator. After the human answers, check exactly the option they chose; the last option is valid when the human explicitly chooses nobody.\n\nCheck exactly one box in each list.\n-->\n\nWho wrote this:\n\n- [ ] A human wrote it.\n- [x] An agent wrote it under close human direction.\n- [ ] An agent wrote it independently, and no human has guided the implementation beyond the initial prompt.\n\nWho answers review comments:\n\n- [x] @BagToad will read and reply directly. Name the account.\n- [ ] An agent will draft replies and @username will read them before they are posted.\n- [ ] Nobody has explicitly committed to replying.\n","created_at":"2026-11-03T17:30:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T17:40:16Z","closed_at":"2026-11-03T17:40:14Z","merged_at":"2026-11-03T17:40:14Z","merge_commit_sha":"eeb44bc432c0107de002dadd34a61b4e2bd15882","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/14918/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/14918/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/issues/14918/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/statuses/f44bd1dcc58a718327a4d1df89ea3d1145c827b2","head":{"label":"cli:bagtoad/gh-help-environment-fix","ref":"bagtoad/gh-help-environment-fix","sha":"f44bd1dcc58a718327a4d1df89ea3d1145c827b2","user":{"login":"cli","id":59704711,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjU5NzA0NzEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59704711?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cli","html_url":"https://github.com/cli","followers_url":"https://api.g